# Template for ZenBI Environment Variables

# --- OpenAI API Key (Required for LLM features) ---
# Replace "your_openai_api_key_here" with your actual OpenAI API Key.
OPENAI_API_KEY="your_openai_api_key_here"


# --- OpenMetadata Configuration (Optional) ---
# If you plan to use OpenMetadata integration, uncomment and fill in these values.
# Refer to OpenMetadata documentation for details on authentication.

# URL of the OpenMetadata server API endpoint.
# Example: OM_SERVER_URL="http://localhost:8585/api"
OM_SERVER_URL=""

# Authentication provider for OpenMetadata.
# Options: "no-auth", "openmetadata", "google"
# Default: OM_AUTH_PROVIDER="no-auth"
OM_AUTH_PROVIDER="no-auth"

# --- Settings for "openmetadata" Auth Provider ---
# JWT Token obtained from your OpenMetadata instance.
# OM_JWT_TOKEN=""

# --- Settings for "google" Auth Provider ---
# This can be the path to your Google service account JSON key file,
# or the content of the key itself, depending on OpenMetadata SDK version and setup.
# Example: OM_SECRET_KEY="/path/to/your/google_service_account.json"
# OM_SECRET_KEY=""

# For some Google auth setups (e.g., Google IdP with custom audience for service accounts),
# this might be the audience URL or a path to a different credentials configuration.
# Consult OpenMetadata documentation for the specific requirements of your Google auth setup.
# Example: OM_GOOGLE_CREDENTIALS_PATH="https_your_google_idp_audience_url"
# OM_GOOGLE_CREDENTIALS_PATH=""
